  <h1>TENCEL™ · Lenzing · production & fibre guide</h1>

  <p><strong>TENCEL™ is a premium textile fibre brand owned by the Austrian company Lenzing AG.</strong> It represents a range of regenerated cellulose fibres, primarily TENCEL™ Lyocell and TENCEL™ Modal.</p>
  <p>These fibres are manufactured using cellulose obtained mainly from wood pulp. The cellulose is processed and regenerated into textile fibres through industrial manufacturing processes.</p>
  <p>TENCEL™ fibres are used in clothing, home textiles and other textile applications because of their softness, smoothness, moisture management and versatility.</p>
  <p>Unlike natural fibres such as cotton, TENCEL™ fibres do not grow directly as textile fibres in nature. Instead, they are manufactured from naturally occurring cellulose.</p>

  <!-- Key points box -->
  <div class="highlight-box">
    <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Key points</h3>
    <ul style="margin-bottom:0.2rem;">
      <li><strong>Brand owner:</strong> Lenzing AG, Austria.</li>
      <li><strong>Main fibre types:</strong> Lyocell and Modal.</li>
      <li><strong>Main raw material:</strong> Wood-based cellulose.</li>
      <li><strong>Applications:</strong> Clothing, bedding, home textiles and fashion products.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:0.8rem; margin-bottom:0;">TENCEL™ is not a generic fibre type; it is a registered brand trademark owned by Lenzing AG.</p>
  </div>

  <p>The generic fibre names are Lyocell and Modal, whereas TENCEL™ identifies Lenzing's branded versions of these fibres.</p>
  <p><strong>For example:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lyocell</strong> = Generic fibre name.</li>
    <li><strong>Modal</strong> = Generic fibre name.</li>
    <li><strong>TENCEL™ Lyocell</strong> = Lenzing's branded Lyocell.</li>
    <li><strong>TENCEL™ Modal</strong> = Lenzing's branded Modal.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This distinction is important in the textile industry because different manufacturers can produce generic Lyocell fibres, but only authorised Lenzing products can be marketed under the TENCEL™ brand.</p>

