  <!-- ===== Lenzing production differentiation ===== -->
  <h2>Lenzing differentiates its production process</h2>
  <p>Lenzing differentiates its production process through its solvent recovery technology, resource-efficient manufacturing systems, responsible raw-material sourcing and efforts to reduce environmental impacts. There are four important aspects.</p>

  <!-- A. Closed-loop -->
  <div class="section-card">
    <h3>A. Closed-loop production system</h3>
    <p>One of the most important features of TENCEL™ Lyocell production is its closed-loop manufacturing process.</p>
    <p><strong>In this process:</strong></p>
    <ol>
      <li>Wood pulp is mixed with water and NMMO solvent.</li>
      <li>The cellulose dissolves to form a spinning solution.</li>
      <li>The solution passes through spinnerets to form fibres.</li>
      <li>The fibres are washed and processed.</li>
      <li>The solvent is recovered and reused in the production process.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>According to Lenzing, more than <strong>99.8%</strong> of the solvent used in its Lyocell production process is recovered and fed back into the production cycle.</p>
    <p class="reference">reflawn.com</p>
  </div>

  <!-- B. Chemical recovery -->
  <div class="section-card">
    <h3>B. Chemical recovery and resource efficiency</h3>
    <p>Lenzing also applies resource-efficient technologies in Modal production. The company focuses on recovering and reusing process chemicals, reducing waste and controlling emissions.</p>
    <p>It is important to distinguish this from Lyocell production: the two fibres use different manufacturing processes, so their chemical recovery systems are not identical.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- C. Responsible wood sourcing -->
  <div class="section-card">
    <h3>C. Responsible wood sourcing</h3>
    <p>Lenzing uses wood from certified or controlled sources for its relevant branded fibres. This approach aims to reduce the risks associated with irresponsible forestry, deforestation and damage to natural ecosystems.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- D. Lower environmental impact -->
  <div class="section-card">
    <h3>D. Lower environmental impact</h3>
    <p>Lenzing reports that TENCEL™ Lyocell and Modal fibres are produced with at least <strong>50% lower carbon emissions and water consumption</strong> compared with generic Lyocell and Modal fibres, respectively.</p>
    <p class="comparison-note">This is a manufacturer-reported comparison, not a universal finding for every Lyocell or Modal producer.</p>
  </div>

